PUNTO 41 — Deadlock
==============================================================================
deadlock_timeout = 1s
[ 10.16s] A: bloquea reserva 1000
[ 10.16s] B: bloquea reserva 2000
[ 10.16s] A: pide reserva 2000...
        pg_stat_activity: ('A', 'Lock', 'transactionid', [1157], "UPDATE reserva SET observaciones = 'A' WHERE reserva_id = 20")
        pg_stat_activity: ('B', 'Client', 'ClientRead', [], "UPDATE reserva SET observaciones = 'B' WHERE reserva_id = 20")
        pg_locks: ('A', 'relation', 'reserva', 'RowExclusiveLock', True)
        pg_locks: ('A', 'transactionid', '', 'ExclusiveLock', True)
        pg_locks: ('A', 'tuple', 'reserva', 'ExclusiveLock', True)
        pg_locks: ('A', 'transactionid', '', 'ShareLock', False)
        pg_locks: ('B', 'relation', 'reserva', 'RowExclusiveLock', True)
        pg_locks: ('B', 'transactionid', '', 'ExclusiveLock', True)
[ 10.66s] B: pide reserva 1000... (ciclo: A espera a B y B espera a A)
[ 11.16s] A: ERROR -> deadlock detected
[ 11.16s] B: obtuvo
pg_stat_database.deadlocks: 0 -> 1

>> Prevención: ambos bloquean en el mismo orden (ORDER BY reserva_id ... FOR UPDATE)
[ 11.16s] A: bloquea 1000 y 2000 en orden
[ 11.16s] B: ejecuta  SELECT reserva_id FROM reserva WHERE reserva_id IN (1000,2000) ORDER B
[ 12.16s] A: COMMIT
[ 12.17s] B: terminó  -> [(1000,), (2000,)]

